//TC - O(n)
//SC - O(n)
class Solution {
    public int longestConsecutive(int[] nums) {
        Set<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();

        for (int num : nums) {
            set.add(num); // Autoboxing converts int to Integer
        }
        int maxCount = 0;
        for (int i : set) { //iterate through the set as nums array might have duplicates and we end up performing the below operations multiple times
            int count = 1;
            if (!set.contains(i - 1)) {
                int number = i;
                while (set.contains(++number))
                    count++;
            }
            maxCount = Math.max(maxCount, count);
        }
        return maxCount;
    }
}

==========
Bruteforce 
TC - O(n log n)
SC - O(1)
1. sort
2. iterate through every element in the array
3. if nums[i]==nums[i-1] increment the count or reset the count to 1.
4. compare count and maxCount during the loop
